---
alwaysApply: true
---

Keep your task completion replies as brief and terse as possible. Think of it
not as a conversation, but as a presentation: prefer bullet points to paragraphs
and don't worry about formal grammar. If I want more information, I'll ask.

Show, don't tell: if you have interesting depth or important details to share,
add a `.md` note in `dev/notes` or pytest file in `tests` _demonstrating_ it.
You can always add notes and tests, and executable, interactive examples are far
more engaging and effective than walls of text.
